=== start ===
# The NPC is walking down the street, handing out flyers supporting the initiative.

#speaker: Player  
Hey, handing out flyers for the initiative? I get why you’re excited, but have you thought about who really benefits from this?

* [Look at the past initiatives. How many of them actually helped people like us?] -> logical_tone
* [It’s heartbreaking. They claim it’s for the people, but it’s always the corporations that profit.] -> emotional_tone
* [Why is it that these policies always seem to favor the richest? Doesn’t that seem suspicious?] -> argumentative_tone
* [I can see why it sounds promising, but maybe we should dig deeper before jumping in.] -> reserved_tone

=== logical_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
Look at the past initiatives. How many of them actually helped people like us? The patterns are hard to ignore.

#speaker: other  
You’re right, but doesn’t it make sense to keep trying? We need something to work.

* [Absolutely, but we need solutions that genuinely prioritize citizens over corporations.] -> logical_tone
* [I want it to work too, but blind hope won’t change the facts.] -> emotional_tone
* [That’s what they count on—us being too desperate to question the flaws.] -> argumentative_tone
* [You’re not wrong. Let’s just make sure this is the right solution.] -> reserved_tone

=== emotional_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
It’s heartbreaking. They claim it’s for the people, but it’s always the corporations that profit. Don’t we deserve better?

#speaker: other  
We do, but maybe this time it’ll be different. Shouldn’t we at least give it a chance?

* [Of course, but let’s make sure this chance doesn’t come at too high a cost.] -> logical_tone
* [I hope you’re right, but it’s hard not to feel betrayed by the system.] -> emotional_tone
* [That’s what they always say—“this time is different”—but it’s just another ploy.] -> argumentative_tone
* [You’re not wrong. Let’s just stay cautious while hoping for the best.] -> reserved_tone

=== argumentative_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
Why is it that these policies always seem to favor the richest? Doesn’t that seem suspicious to you?

#speaker: other  
I guess, but maybe those benefits will eventually trickle down to everyone.

* [That’s been debunked time and again. The wealth rarely trickles down.] -> logical_tone
* [How long are we supposed to wait for that trickle to happen?] -> emotional_tone
* [That’s the lie they sell us to keep us compliant. We deserve better.] -> argumentative_tone
* [You’re not wrong to hope for that, but let’s ensure this is truly fair.] -> reserved_tone

=== reserved_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
I can see why it sounds promising, but maybe we should dig deeper before jumping in. Sometimes these things aren’t as they seem.

#speaker: other  
You’re probably right. It’s worth taking a closer look before fully committing.

* [Exactly. Real benefits won’t require so much convincing—they’ll speak for themselves.] -> logical_tone
* [I just want to make sure we don’t regret trusting another empty promise.] -> emotional_tone
* [We owe it to ourselves to question who truly benefits from this.] -> argumentative_tone
* [Take your time. I’m here if you want to talk more about it.] -> reserved_tone
